<%# The row's figure, as its own element so a save can replace it.

    Without this the column goes stale the moment a grade changes: the autosave PATCH returns a
    turbo_stream that replaced only the buttons, so the money on screen would have disagreed with the
    inputs beside it until a reload. A figure that is quietly wrong is worse than no figure.

    Only the number, because the column is right-aligned with tabular-nums and an annotation in it
    pushes the digits off the edge they align to. %>
<%= tag.td id: dom_id(entry, :earnings),
           class: "table-body-cell table-body-cell-right whitespace-nowrap font-medium",
           data: { testid: "row-earnings" } do %>
  <%= number_to_currency(earnings.for(entry).total / 100.0) %>
<% end %>
